Z||000000||fiero56||05-21-2001||10:15 PM||||I decided to try and glue the sides of the rally gauges on my '86 back into place yesterday. I put loads of bonding cement(or similar, I don't remember exactly) between the peeling vinyl and the inner structure on driver and passenger sides. Let it cure for over 30hours, took the clamp off, re-installed the unit, and just went out to the garage to see how the glue was holding. The passenger side is already beginning to let loose, only 6 hours after taking the clamp off.<P>What do others use to fix this problem. I tried to get as much foam out of the way as possible, but it still didn't hold.||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||05-21-2001||11:10 PM||||Here's a few from the search:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009442.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009442.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007305.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007305.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-004145.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-004145.html</A> <P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||05-21-2001||11:39 PM||||i didtn read the links above posted.  however,  what i used on mine was any type of crazy glue and an accelerator.  i found them at a hoppy shop for a couple bucks.  i didnt use them on the rally gauges because they didnt need it.  but i did use it on just about every other piece of vinyl in my car.  for example.  the shift surround.  i cut out the foam on the edges.  then cleaned it with a paint thinner(it was available) then applied the glue,  i pressed it together good with a straight edge and sprayed the accelerator on it and only had to hold it for about 10 sec.  the key for me was to be patient and only doin about an inch at a time.  good luck.. if you want i can get some picks of what i mean by all this nonsense.  im really slow at work right nwo and im workin on a couple more.  good luck||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||05-22-2001||03:10 AM||||Drew, if you can hang on til I get back there (about three weeks or so - I need to do some things to my GT I drove back there) I will show you how to fix that curling thing .......... You have seen both my gold and med. red GTs and I repaired the trim on both of them...........if you can't hang on that long, call me (toll free) at 866-534-8486 and I'll step ya through it.........<P>Terry<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">              </A><P>87 GT - 2.8L Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - 3.4L Blue 5-speed Getrag<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag<BR>88 Coupe - 2.5L Red automatic||||reg||1
